    ["He was the best Clown, needing no thick oil paint to offer the most exaggerated smile. This smile was like a perfect mask, fitting his face seamlessly. Please stretch the corners of your mouth to the maximum; the smile was impeccable, even if his eyes were completely hollow. \n His performance was unmatched, his absurdity so laughable. Every move he made could touch the most precise nerves of the audience, and every blunder could trigger hysterical laughter from the crowd. Children loved him, adults found an outlet for the pressures of life in him, and he brought joy to the whole world with his own smile! \n However, when the curtain fell and the laughter dispersed, facing himself in the mirror who was always smiling while alone, he could only respond with silence and an exaggerated smile. \n The final stage arrived; he replaced the poisoned wine the monarch gave the jester in the story with real poisoned wine and drank it in one gulp. When he fell with a smile, thunderous cheers and laughter erupted throughout the arena. \n \n The show... has come to a curtain call... Wishing you all again... to be happy forever."] = "He was the best Клоун, needing no thick oil paint to offer the most exaggerated smile. This smile was like a perfect mask, fitting his face seamlessly. Please stretch the corners of your mouth to the maximum; the smile was impeccable, even if his eyes were completely hollow. \n His performance was unmatched, his absurdity so laughable. Every move he made could touch the most precise nerves of the audience, and every blunder could trigger hysterical laughter from the crowd. Children loved him, adults found an outlet for the pressures of life in him, and he brought joy to the whole world with his own smile! \n However, when the curtain fell and the laughter dispersed, facing himself in the mirror who was always smiling while alone, he could only respond with silence and an exaggerated smile. \n The final stage arrived; he replaced the poisoned wine the monarch gave the jester in the story with real poisoned wine and drank it in one gulp. When he fell with a smile, thunderous cheers and laughter erupted throughout the arena. \n \n The show... has come to a curtain call... Wishing you all again... to be happy forever.",
